1
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:24,297
All right, enough.

2
00:00:24,380 --> 00:00:25,737
Something's going on here.

3
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:30,408
I felt like someone's eyes have been on
me all morning watching my every move.

4
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:34,650
Why?

5
00:00:34,733 --> 00:00:35,563
Clearly I'm alone.

6
00:00:38,460 --> 00:00:40,857
Nobody could have followed
me all the way out here.

7
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:42,757
I'm out in the middle of nowhere.

8
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:46,200
But I can't shake the
feeling that someone's here!

9
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:48,880
Damn my imagination.

10
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:52,127
Must be the heat playing
tricks with my mind.

11
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:00,246
Well, aren't you a sharp one?

12
00:01:00,460 --> 00:01:02,197
You somehow sensed my presence?

13
00:01:02,280 --> 00:01:04,217
Although I was engaging
my skills of stealth.

14
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:05,340
this entire time.

15
00:01:05,540 --> 00:01:07,380
Even while bats can't do that.

16
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:09,537
Why the hell are you following me?

17
00:01:09,620 --> 00:01:11,385
I've got no business with you.

18
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:12,820
Oh, I'm not following.

19
00:01:13,160 --> 00:01:15,395
I'm in the business of capturing, see?

20
00:01:15,620 --> 00:01:18,677
Our army would like to ask you
some questions about Strazo.

21
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:19,960
Joseph Joestar!

22
00:01:21,440 --> 00:01:24,087
Straitzo, why would you
be interested in him?

23
00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:26,320
And who is our army?

24
00:01:54,960 --> 00:01:57,760
Thank you.

25
00:02:57,960 --> 00:03:02,417
By your accent, the cut of your face,
and your smell, I'd guess you're German.

26
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:04,057
I want to know!

27
00:03:04,140 --> 00:03:07,577
What business a thug like you has with
either Straight So or Speed Wagon,

28
00:03:07,660 --> 00:03:09,917
but if you're not Gonna say anything,

29
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,257
I don't mind having to beat
some answers out of you.

30
00:03:12,340 --> 00:03:14,477
You think you can take On the blade of SS

31
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:16,837
Commander Jonoban with
just your bare hands,

32
00:03:16,920 --> 00:03:17,750
little boy?

33
00:03:17,833 --> 00:03:23,700
I'm almost I was insulted, but since
you insist, I'm happy to oblige! Great!

34
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:27,313
But how about I give you back
your flea-ridden magic rag?

35
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:37,200
Cactus needles!

36
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:46,350
Victory!

37
00:03:46,880 --> 00:03:50,437
I really thought that you were going
to give me more of a challenge there.

38
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:52,049
What happened, little boy?

39
00:03:52,420 --> 00:03:53,600
Repeat after me.

40
00:03:53,860 --> 00:03:57,684
I never should have challenged
your superior power, Hear Donovan.

41
00:03:57,860 --> 00:03:58,690
I...

42
00:03:58,773 --> 00:04:03,320
I never should have challenged
your superior power. What's that?

43
00:04:03,640 --> 00:04:04,920
I can't hear you.

44
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:08,060
I underestimated your etiquette.

45
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:11,097
You really are quite the
gentleman for letting me rest

46
00:04:11,180 --> 00:04:13,757
right here and giving me these
moments to recover safely.

47
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:15,840
What are you talking about?

48
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:17,360
Recover safely?

49
00:04:17,780 --> 00:04:19,898
Have you lost your mind, little boy?

50
00:04:20,020 --> 00:04:21,357
Wait a sec, what's this?

51
00:04:21,440 --> 00:04:22,697
What's up for this cactus?

52
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:24,545
You should take a closer look.

53
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:38,900
That cactus was my goal
all along, Hear Donovan.

54
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:42,457
Cacti are made up of nearly 95 % water,

55
00:04:42,540 --> 00:04:45,517
and they're known to be
fabulous conductors of Hamon.

56
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:48,440
Now then, repeat after me, Hear Donovan.

57
00:04:48,860 --> 00:04:51,448
I promise to tell Joseph
Joestar everything.

58
00:04:55,780 --> 00:04:56,700
Okay, then.

59
00:04:57,020 --> 00:04:59,080
When Speedwagon's body disappeared,

60
00:04:59,360 --> 00:05:03,242
I swore to myself that I would
never give up hope, no matter what.

61
00:05:04,640 --> 00:05:06,560
Turns out he was safe all along.

62
00:05:06,860 --> 00:05:09,880
Man, it's nice to hear some
good news for a change.

63
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:13,200
I can't wait to tell Granny Iran.

64
00:05:13,380 --> 00:05:15,615
She'll be so happy to hear about this.

65
00:05:16,340 --> 00:05:21,157
Although, there's no way of telling how the
Germans have actually been treating him.

66
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:22,070
Regardless,

67
00:05:22,260 --> 00:05:27,100
I'll bring him home, and Granny Irina's
smile will shine like the midday sun.

68
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:34,150
Hey!

69
00:05:34,380 --> 00:05:35,940
Don't leave him!

70
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:43,080
Look, Major von Stroheim!

71
00:05:43,300 --> 00:05:45,535
The pittal shell is starting to crack!

72
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:48,717
It's currently holding the
blood of five prisoners.

73
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:51,797
We still don't know what
its full capabilities are.

74
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:55,880
Feeding it anymore could push it
beyond our established safety zone.

75
00:05:57,160 --> 00:06:00,631
I'm curious how the blood was
extracted in the first place.

76
00:06:01,020 --> 00:06:02,797
No, wait, I don't want to know.

77
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:05,880
I can imagine what sort of
things you came up with.

78
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:15,182
Oh, Speedwagon.

79
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:19,760
No need to look so pale.

80
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:22,737
I told you from the start
there was nothing to fear.

81
00:06:22,820 --> 00:06:24,173
Stop being so arrogant!

82
00:06:24,260 --> 00:06:26,378
You've no idea what he's capable of!

83
00:06:26,620 --> 00:06:27,820
Relax, old man.

84
00:06:28,420 --> 00:06:30,500
That test chamber is impenetrable.

85
00:06:31,260 --> 00:06:34,680
It has iron walls nearly 20 inches thick.

86
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:39,567
It's equipped with flamethrowers, machine
guns, and explosives if we need them.

87
00:06:40,180 --> 00:06:42,977
I shouldn't be surprised
that all of your courage

88
00:06:43,060 --> 00:06:45,497
doesn't even add up to what
I have in my little finger,

89
00:06:45,580 --> 00:06:46,410
you coward!

90
00:06:47,340 --> 00:06:49,457
Want to know what I think, Speedwagon?

91
00:06:49,540 --> 00:06:51,737
I think that thing is simply a statue of

92
00:06:51,820 --> 00:06:54,740
petrified caveman bones
that's wasting my time!

93
00:06:58,220 --> 00:06:59,740
Danger! He's erupting!

94
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:02,950
It's blood!

95
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:06,017
That blood it took in is
spraying out everywhere!

96
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:07,380
I can't see a thing!

97
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:09,525
Activate the sprinkler system!

98
00:07:35,660 --> 00:07:37,757
His outer layer is transforming!

99
00:07:37,840 --> 00:07:40,360
It looks like it's morphing into flesh!

100
00:07:40,920 --> 00:07:42,440
He's trying to move!

101
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:44,260
I think he's alive!

102
00:07:48,620 --> 00:07:50,520
Well, he'll need a name.

103
00:07:50,700 --> 00:07:52,920
Something better than the Pillar Man.

104
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:57,134
As his new godfather, I suppose
this task falls onto me.

105
00:07:57,440 --> 00:07:58,500
Let me see.

106
00:07:59,340 --> 00:08:01,800
I'll name him after the Mexican winds.

107
00:08:01,960 --> 00:08:03,842
He shall be known as San Viento.

108
00:08:06,380 --> 00:08:09,140
Look, he's trying to stand.

109
00:08:09,660 --> 00:08:11,800
Rise before us.

110
00:08:12,060 --> 00:08:15,160
Rise up and show us what you are made of.

111
00:08:15,540 --> 00:08:16,520
San Viento!

112
00:08:58,420 --> 00:08:59,780
You see that?

113
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:04,080
San Viento might have a future
They're doing comedy in the cabaret.

114
00:09:04,260 --> 00:09:08,100
The ultimate organism, and
more like the ultimate idiot.

115
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:10,357
What do you think there, Speedwagon?

116
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:12,700
He's got the brains of a feral animal.

117
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:15,057
He's trying to smell his way around.

118
00:09:15,140 --> 00:09:17,360
He's really just a primitive man.

119
00:09:20,120 --> 00:09:21,660
This is a farce.

120
00:09:21,920 --> 00:09:25,449
Regardless, let's just move on
and assume he made the masks.

121
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:27,922
You there, start the experiment.

122
00:09:28,180 --> 00:09:31,300
Somebody open the door to
the next chamber. Yes, sir.

123
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:40,150
What?

124
00:09:40,233 --> 00:09:42,480
What's that supposed to be? A prisoner.

125
00:09:42,860 --> 00:09:45,154
Well, a prisoner with a mask, actually.

126
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:47,280
Is that a vampire?

127
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:50,880
Only a few days ago,
that thing was a feeble,

128
00:09:51,020 --> 00:09:53,549
toothless old man
knocking on death's door.

129
00:09:53,740 --> 00:09:57,120
We still haven't fed him
today, so he must be thirsty.

130
00:09:57,380 --> 00:09:59,757
I think he'll go straight for the attack.

131
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:00,957
Who will win?

132
00:10:01,040 --> 00:10:03,140
I can hardly wait.

133
00:10:07,600 --> 00:10:08,960
What? That's all?

134
00:10:09,100 --> 00:10:10,637
He didn't even put up a fight.

135
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:13,040
He's an ordinary man after all.

136
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:16,797
We don't have any other subjects
for this test, Major von Stroheim.

137
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:20,537
We planted explosives in the prisoner's
head for this exact situation.

138
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:23,317
Just give us the word and we'll
activate them immediately.

139
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:24,600
Major? Fine.

140
00:10:35,640 --> 00:10:36,800
Wait! Stop!

141
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:39,920
I rescind the order! His jaw! Look!

142
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:41,857
What's happening there with his jaw?

143
00:10:41,940 --> 00:10:42,800
His hands!

144
00:10:43,040 --> 00:10:44,000
His arms!

145
00:10:44,160 --> 00:10:45,925
What's going on with his arms?

146
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:50,640
I'd given him up for dead
in the beginning, but look!

147
00:10:51,020 --> 00:10:53,860
San Viento is somehow
absorbing the prisoner!

148
00:10:59,560 --> 00:11:02,080
He's pulling him straight into his body.

149
00:11:02,280 --> 00:11:03,760
He's devouring him!

150
00:11:07,180 --> 00:11:09,340
What a marvelous creature!

151
00:11:09,780 --> 00:11:12,800
The masked man was no
more than fodder for him.

152
00:11:13,100 --> 00:11:15,600
San Viento feeds with his entire body.

153
00:11:15,780 --> 00:11:17,760
So nothing is lost.

154
00:11:17,920 --> 00:11:22,096
He can absorb every bit of his prey's
life force down to the last drop.

155
00:11:23,860 --> 00:11:24,960
He ate him.

156
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:26,944
He actually ate the masked man.

157
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:29,029
How is that even possible?

158
00:11:30,240 --> 00:11:31,460
Oh, now look.

159
00:11:31,740 --> 00:11:33,440
He's grown something.

160
00:11:34,300 --> 00:11:35,400
Get a grip.

161
00:11:35,680 --> 00:11:38,237
As long as he's still in that
chamber, he can't hurt you.

162
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:40,677
He just gained a little
weight after his feeding.

163
00:11:40,760 --> 00:11:41,760
That's all it is.

164
00:11:42,460 --> 00:11:43,777
His intelligence.

165
00:11:43,860 --> 00:11:45,742
And what about his intelligence?

166
00:11:46,460 --> 00:11:49,440
What level of thought
is he capable of? Huh?

167
00:11:54,080 --> 00:11:58,380
Me, Major von Star, Stroheim. What?

168
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:02,080
But how did he, he said,
how did he know my name?

169
00:12:02,420 --> 00:12:06,244
He's not even supposed to be able
to hear anything from in there!

170
00:12:17,120 --> 00:12:18,340
There it is.

171
00:12:18,580 --> 00:12:21,180
According to my dangling
cactus pal Donoban,

172
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:25,137
the underground facility I'm looking
for is hidden down there somewhere.

173
00:12:25,220 --> 00:12:28,780
If he was telling the truth,
Speedwagon should be inside.

174
00:12:29,280 --> 00:12:31,868
So now, where am I
supposed to get in there?

175
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:36,100
Vegetables, canned
goods, meat, thyme, eggs.

176
00:12:36,300 --> 00:12:39,888
Looks like you've got a nice
basket of food there, all right.

177
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:44,540
Now then, it's time for the frisking.

178
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:49,820
Oh, come on now, stop making that face.

179
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:51,697
You can give me a little smile.

180
00:12:51,780 --> 00:12:53,545
Lift up your skirts and smile.

181
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:02,940
You're cleared to go!

182
00:13:03,480 --> 00:13:04,310
NEXT!

183
00:13:04,580 --> 00:13:07,698
All I've got under my skirt
is more tequila, big boy!

184
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:10,273
Is it alright to bring that through too?

185
00:13:13,580 --> 00:13:15,060
Hands up in the air!

186
00:13:15,280 --> 00:13:17,297
Any funny moves and we'll shoot you dead!

187
00:13:17,380 --> 00:13:18,210
Mwah!

188
00:13:18,293 --> 00:13:19,123
Put your guns down!

189
00:13:19,206 --> 00:13:20,277
I haven't done anything!

190
00:13:20,360 --> 00:13:21,889
That's a funny move there!

191
00:13:22,180 --> 00:13:23,010
FIRE!

192
00:13:23,280 --> 00:13:24,110
No!

193
00:13:24,240 --> 00:13:25,317
Please don't shoot!

194
00:13:25,400 --> 00:13:28,377
I'm not moving it, but I've
got my hands in the air!

195
00:13:28,460 --> 00:13:29,477
Alright, damn it!

196
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:30,617
You Germans are so smart!

197
00:13:30,700 --> 00:13:34,660
You saw through my disguise
almost immediately are you crazy?

198
00:13:34,880 --> 00:13:36,517
Of course we saw through that thing.

199
00:13:36,600 --> 00:13:39,377
You're disgusting Even
my big sister isn't as

200
00:13:39,460 --> 00:13:41,637
ugly as you when we used
her to plant the fields.

201
00:13:41,720 --> 00:13:44,277
She was an ox you should
have spent more time

202
00:13:44,360 --> 00:13:46,477
in front of the mirror
this morning big sissy!

203
00:13:46,560 --> 00:13:47,720
What was that?

204
00:14:02,060 --> 00:14:04,580
Well, that was disappointingly easy.

205
00:14:05,140 --> 00:14:09,400
If I can get this thing to fit,
this uniform should work nicely.

206
00:14:10,300 --> 00:14:11,130
What?

207
00:14:11,213 --> 00:14:12,043
What's going on?

208
00:14:12,140 --> 00:14:13,220
I don't know.

209
00:14:13,780 --> 00:14:14,680
You don't know?

210
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:15,961
Virtue watching?

211
00:14:16,340 --> 00:14:19,257
Major von Stroheim, I only
looked away for a moment.

212
00:14:19,340 --> 00:14:20,634
Surely you understand.

213
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:22,937
I mean, you were here as well, right?

214
00:14:23,020 --> 00:14:24,637
Everybody here was watching.

215
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:27,600
It just happens that nobody saw anything.

216
00:14:31,880 --> 00:14:33,440
Put that coffee down!

217
00:14:35,640 --> 00:14:37,500
It was only for a moment.

218
00:14:38,060 --> 00:14:40,766
I took my eyes off him
for just a few seconds.

219
00:14:40,860 --> 00:14:42,036
That's all, I swear.

220
00:14:42,160 --> 00:14:43,320
It makes no sense.

221
00:14:43,540 --> 00:14:44,857
I mean, my vision is perfect.

222
00:14:44,940 --> 00:14:47,617
We all have a clear view, but
we don't know what happened.

223
00:14:47,700 --> 00:14:48,935
This is unbelievable!

224
00:14:50,840 --> 00:14:55,260
The chamber is completely sealed, and
still the subject managed to escape!

225
00:14:55,540 --> 00:14:58,011
None of the walls show any sign of damage.

226
00:14:58,700 --> 00:15:00,197
I don't care what you saw.

227
00:15:00,280 --> 00:15:03,637
I want him found keep in mind
that he may have concealed himself

228
00:15:03,720 --> 00:15:08,017
somewhere inside the chamber simply
cut off the oxygen supply in there.

229
00:15:08,100 --> 00:15:10,982
He'll turn up when he
finds out he can't breathe!

230
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:15,101
The recorded film is now ready for
your viewing major von Stroheim.

231
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:16,697
What are you waiting for set it up?

232
00:15:16,780 --> 00:15:17,610
Yes, sir

233
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:20,500
Roll the film

234
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:33,820
See that?

235
00:15:33,980 --> 00:15:35,745
He's running towards the wall.

236
00:15:35,860 --> 00:15:37,040
Yeah, but why?

237
00:15:48,740 --> 00:15:50,020
Was he's lost?

238
00:15:50,180 --> 00:15:53,560
He's squeezing himself
into the ventilation ducts!

239
00:15:53,700 --> 00:15:56,257
Those sluts are less than two inches tall!

240
00:15:56,340 --> 00:16:01,120
How the hell could anyone possibly stop
an entire body to a cap that small?

241
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:03,030
Incredible!

242
00:16:03,280 --> 00:16:05,560
He didn't simply dislocate his joints.

243
00:16:05,820 --> 00:16:08,797
He somehow disassembled
his entire skeleton so

244
00:16:08,880 --> 00:16:11,762
that he could completely
alter his shape at will!

245
00:16:21,780 --> 00:16:23,317
You know what this means.

246
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:27,988
He is now wandering around freely somewhere
in your face's ventilation system.

247
00:16:28,500 --> 00:16:31,737
San Viento already know your
name somehow, Major von Stroheim,

248
00:16:31,820 --> 00:16:33,526
and I think I might know how.

249
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:38,367
The only way that would be possible is
if he heard your name through the vents.

250
00:16:41,140 --> 00:16:43,740
The vents lead directly into this room?

251
00:16:44,020 --> 00:16:47,961
You, soldier, turn around and move
away from that vent immediately.

252
00:16:48,100 --> 00:16:48,980
Go, you idiot!

253
00:17:01,440 --> 00:17:02,270
It's him!

254
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:03,301
It's San Viento!

255
00:17:05,080 --> 00:17:06,433
What's happening to me?

256
00:17:06,600 --> 00:17:08,080
Major Von Stroheim!

257
00:17:08,820 --> 00:17:09,777
What's happening?

258
00:17:09,860 --> 00:17:11,213
Where did everybody go?

259
00:17:11,480 --> 00:17:13,360
And why is it so dark in here?

260
